{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>חכלילי.</b> A term of redness, as its Targum renders; and so ״לְמִי חַכְלִילוּת עֵינָיִם״ (Proverbs 23) — for so is the way of wine drinkers, their eyes grow red." "<b>From milk.</b> From an abundance of milk — that there be in his land good pasture for flocks of sheep. And so the meaning of the verse: redness of eyes will be from an abundance of wine, and whiteness of teeth from an abundance of milk. And according to its Targum, עינים is a term for mountains, for from there one looks out to the distance. And further, he translated it another way: a term for springs and the flow of winepresses — נַעֲווֹהִי — his winepresses; and it is an Aramaic term in tractate Avodah Zarah (74a): נַעֲוָא אַרְתְּחוֹ יְחַוְּרָן בִּקְעָתֵהּ — the Targum of שִׁנַּיִם: a term for the teeth of the rocks."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:07.364855578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}